 "notes": "PACKET ANOMALY: the F1 image file shows paper Fig. 1 (left) AND Fig. 2 (right) side by side; packet F2 path is a bare directory; the images folder holds an unlisted file 813100...jpg that is a near-duplicate of the same composite. Figure ids here follow the image file, so Fig. 2 readings carry F1. Figures opened: F1, 813100 (duplicate), F3, F4. Structure-heavy mechanism paper: no measured property; PRP/behavior_class b25 is argued from the imaged defect geometry. The spine runs linearly core -> escort phasons -> R slab -> mechanism. Evidence is interpretive: the tilings are hand-superimposed on HAADF images, so every STR claim depends on b7 (tiling validation). Only one core is imaged; representativeness is assumed ('typical area'). The Burgers circuit (F3) is a construction on the image: typed derives+replot_derived_series then measure_feature_metric; there is no dedicated op, and one use does not justify one. Lost: supplementary contrast-extinction analysis, the 1,500-atom count derivation, the phase-diagram argument detail."
}